#
# char_server manifest -- the policy for the task that owns the keyboard and
# the serial lines (#744).
#
# 🔴 IT HAD NONE, AND NEEDED ONE THE MOMENT SUBSCRIBING TO REVOCATIONS DID.
# char_server acquires nothing: it verifies the tokens its clients bring with
# the kernel (urmach_cap_verify) and keeps a keyboard subscription per token.
# What it asks cap_server for is to be told when one of those is revoked, so
# that a revoked token stops receiving keys -- and that is a permission now,
# granted by a manifest and asked for on the per-task port bootstrap gives a
# task that ships one.  A server with no policy file has no such port.

name char_server

# RESOURCE_REVOKE_NOTICES (11), any, CAP_OP_REVOKE_SUBSCRIBE (0x1).
required 11 any 0x1
